; Four rejections: one each for the empty and repeated lists, two for the
; overlap (`[b c]` repeats `b`, and the scalar `b` repeats it again). The
; paths are the loader's `[<form> variant when]` shape. No
; `variant_key_collision`: the three overlapping variants declare three
; distinct keys — the value-level overlap is the whole finding.
;
; No document body: a manifest carrying `invalid_manifest` errors does not
; register its forms, so any instance below would add an `unknown_form`
; that says nothing about this case.
(diagnostics
  (diagnostic :code invalid_manifest :path [empty variant when])
  (diagnostic :code invalid_manifest :path [repeat variant when])
  (diagnostic :code invalid_manifest :path [overlap variant when])
  (diagnostic :code invalid_manifest :path [overlap variant when]))
